# Line endings in the files that the tests read.
#
# The converter reads a line ending as a break in a paragraph, so a test
# compares the lines that come back. A Windows checkout converts a text file to
# CRLF by default. The converter accepts CRLF, but a test that holds its
# expected output in a file then compares bytes that the checkout changed.
#
# Pin the text files to LF on every platform. This is not a preference about
# editors. It is the condition under which the tests mean anything on Windows.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.astro text eol=lf

# Binary, and never converted.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
